# scripts/lineark-checksums.sha256 — operator-reviewed sha256 pins for the
# optional `lineark` CLI, consumed by scripts/install-lineark.{sh,ps1}.
#
# Upstream (github.com/flipbit03/lineark) publishes tagged releases carrying raw
# binaries and NO checksum manifest, so integrity has to be pinned here. Each
# line records a sha256 an operator computed locally from the official release
# asset after reviewing that release. A tag with no entry is an UNVETTED release:
# the installer refuses it outright rather than downloading on trust.
#
# Format: `<sha256>  <tag>/<asset>` — two spaces, one entry per line. Lines
# starting with `#` and blank lines are ignored by the lookup. Two entries for
# the same key with DIFFERENT hashes are a refusal, not a race: the file would no
# longer say which artifact is vetted.
#
# ADDING a release is the vet-pin-checksum-smoke procedure documented in
# linear/linear-setup.md §3.2 ("Updating / re-vetting a new release").
#
# KEEPING old tags listed is deliberate — it is what makes rollback work
# (`LINEARK_VERSION=<old-tag> bash scripts/install-lineark.sh`).
#
# REMOVING an entry is the REVOCATION mechanism, and the only one. When a
# release is withdrawn upstream or found vulnerable, delete its lines here: the
# installer then refuses that tag as an unvetted release, so no operator can roll
# back onto it by accident. Removal is therefore a deliberate security action,
# not tidying — say why in the commit message.

